==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Geishun Mikan''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Unlike most other [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusives, this unit can't really be used in her first form. She costs the same and has the same recharge in exchange for a 1 second faster attack rate, lower stats and much lower critical chance.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Geishun Mikan has disturbingly powerful stats for a unit carrying a 50% [[Critical Hit]] chance, able to wipe a 300% magnification [[Sir Metal Seal]] off of the battlefield with merely a few Catseyes used! To balance this, Geishun has significant drawbacks going against her raw critical damage. For one, her TBA is nearly 10 seconds long, so her criticals come rare and few. This combined with her massive blindspot, with [[Super Metal Hippoe]] only rubbing salt in the wound, means that crowd-control support such as [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster Cat]] and [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster Cat]]/[[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]] is critical, pun unintentional. With the right synergy and strategy, and some luck, Geishun can cut through Metal enemies like butter.

Meanwhile, her sniper usage is fair despite the existence of [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] and arguably [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]]. Treat her like a roided [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] who snipes backliners with her good range and wide pierce. Her [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] isn't a direct counter to [[Wave Attack]] enemies but rather protection in backliner stages that happen to contain Waves. Just remember that her DPS fluctuates based on how often she lands critical hits.

{{Job|Classification = Sniper & Critter}}

