==Trivia==
*Unlike all other [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusives, this unit has orange eyes rather than blue.
**Additionally, its summoning cost is the same in both forms, instead of having two forms with separate usage.
*Both forms carry a satsuma (a type of mandarin orange) known in Japanese as [[wikipedia:Citrus unshiu|Mikan]]. Satsumas are commonly eaten during the winter/new year.
*The orange Cat that Hatsuyume Mikan carries has a stem that can be seen in both of her icons that doesn't appear in-battle, however an unused sprite for it does exist within her spritesheet.
*Like with her [[Natsu Mikan (PC Uber Rare Cat)|summer variant]], the frond leaflets are both shorter and thicker in Geishun Mikan's in-battle appearance compared to how they are in her icons. Another change is that Mikan's hair pins were moved lower, now appearing to be set behind her head instead of in her hair bun. The shine on her bangs also differs between her icons and in-battle appearance.
*Her first form's name may be a reference to the vocaloid [[wikipedia:Hatsune Miku|Hatsune Miku]]. The use of katakana (ミカン) rather than kanji (蜜柑) to write the name "Mikan" further supports this point. Additionally, both forms also sit on top of [[wikipedia:Kagami mochi|Kagami mochi]], which also may reference another set of vocaloids – the [[wikipedia:Kagamine Rin/Len|Kagamine twins]].

